 in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-3.$ To see this clearly, note that we can write the parabola as follows:\n\n$$\ny=4(x-(-5))^{2}-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4018be9-18ab-5854-87d6-149238ab6f53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09054d20-782a-5afe-b1b2-eaca3c0030a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561610} {:answer/id #uuid "20ce2090-0c6f-539b-b740-0c9d5fb8317e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561672} {:answer/id #uuid "57570136-28db-5e5c-8a9a-e69c65121f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561796} {:answer/id #uuid "704151e4-4e4a-50e3-af7c-6a6a09e0a63b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561859} {:answer/id #uuid "d85316aa-884f-5d60-82ac-c2726a928dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d85316aa-884f-5d60-82ac-c2726a928dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562122} :answer-field/id #uuid "5210d6fc-62ed-5538-bea7-c1bbadf45b6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8594afb6-5972-53f6-b33b-4159f91dec13" :question/math-academy-id "q-106236" :question/problem "What is the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=6(x-4)^{2}-7?$" :question/worked-solution "The axis of symmetry of the parabola is the vertical line that passes through the vertex of the parabola. To find the axis of symmetry, we need to compute the $x$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=6(x-4)^{2}-7\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=4$ and $k=-7.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(4,-7),$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4018be9-18ab-5854-87d6-149238ab6f53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21669d3a-c99e-5817-8422-8a8a8b99ba68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561675} {:answer/id #uuid "7b710b6f-61b8-5e9c-8ffe-1c74eaf6ed79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561888} {:answer/id #uuid "d67dfafe-8a15-5d5d-81e0-c717b5c61b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562117} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ace4ce-5bed-5b10-92a9-f5b249d03240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562158} {:answer/id #uuid "ede5968c-5139-5c22-bc07-23de2e6c692f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ede5968c-5139-5c22-bc07-23de2e6c692f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562176} :answer-field/id #uuid "70a49d6f-ce20-599d-ab73-c3287c4c7f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0632da5c-9a68-5b87-b79c-de6c52b69ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-106238" :question/problem "What is the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x-6)^{2}+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The axis of symmetry of the parabola is the vertical line that passes through the vertex of the parabola. To find the axis of symmetry, we need to compute the $x$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=(x-6)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=6$ and $k=1.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(6,1),$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4018be9-18ab-5854-87d6-149238ab6f53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b1f8de-8d43-5644-aa6c-61d05e79f17e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561592} {:answer/id #uuid "2b40f85a-bfbb-5db0-b492-d54461a22cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561694} {:answer/id #uuid "48402f88-74b4-5f3b-9927-2ab9ef4eaf26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561764} {:answe