 the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=-(x+2)^{2}+3\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-2$ and $k=3.$ To see this clearly, note that we can write the parabola as follows:\n\n$$\ny=-(x-(-2))^{2}+3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4018be9-18ab-5854-87d6-149238ab6f53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3316555a-d4cb-5dcc-940e-1a646035997f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561716} {:answer/id #uuid "6505d53f-2536-5e4f-8f25-1670530079a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561831} {:answer/id #uuid "baac87ea-9f41-579b-937f-e5308ffecab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562061} {:answer/id #uuid "f131f073-0c8a-5b82-8169-39a7ca28063f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562183} {:answer/id #uuid "f5007008-b562-58e5-af82-94d41f9658b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3316555a-d4cb-5dcc-940e-1a646035997f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561716} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2724c69-1aad-5ad0-812d-b8b17762a961" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29b03696-3c9f-5636-9c19-2a6a7c7c486b" :question/math-academy-id "q-85125" :question/problem "What is the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x+2)^{2}-5?$" :question/worked-solution "The axis of symmetry of the parabola is the vertical line that passes through the vertex of the parabola. To find the axis of symmetry, we need to compute the $x$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=(x+2)^{2}-5\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-2$ and $k=-5.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-2,-5),$ and the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97f63d2a-8297-5034-96e0-ecae4f62c5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum or Maximum Value of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac0d35b-4ef7-58d9-ba51-feda32aabec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561616} {:answer/id #uuid "19c36781-3c1e-5113-9ce9-df536c37ec80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561654} {:answer/id #uuid "494482c5-bc27-566a-9dcd-a7be70402440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561768} {:answer/id #uuid "6b340ba5-0086-5d04-b040-68dac39650de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561850} {:answer/id #uuid "d14661e2-0f7a-555a-81e1-ef563d09f2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b340ba5-0086-5d04-b040-68dac39650de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561850} :answer-field/id #uuid "215a268f-4f2f-5250-bcca-1acc469f1269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d0de4b8-6fc5-5dcf-a220-ce0c3dea2116" :question/math-academy-id "q-85131" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of the parabola $y=-4(x+5)^{2}-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The maximum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=-4(x+5)^{2}-3\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-3.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-3),$ and its maximum value is $-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97f63d2a-8297-5034-96e0-ecae4f62c5a8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum or Maximum Value of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac1c35a-bafe-5ad3-b28d-d8b0ce41d37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561617} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2b7bc8-41fc-550c-b56c-d1d9568a0eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561772} {:answer/id #uuid "58805847-e5ac-5345-89bb-b21c27b57781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561799} {:answer/id #uuid "627534d8-9259-57c6-8e45-94a1948f847d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561821} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1bf146-5664-5571-a9a3-eb3c65161d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a2b7bc8-41fc-550c-b56c-d1d9568a0eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561772} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed326daf-c793-50e2-8958-689529016221" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44eed42c-2275-58db-b76f-79ce8ef867da" :question/math-academy-id "q-85134" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d805cc4e6c4b817cc4a00d4cccfca59a8bb89ba49442b01deaed3ec75c2ffc1b.png)\n\nFind the minimum value of the parabola $y=3(x+5)^{2}-6$, sketched above." :question/worked-solution "The minimum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=3(x+5)^{2}-6\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-6.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-6),$ and its minimum value is $-6.$"}]}
